{"summary":"The little stint (Calidris minuta) (or Erolia minuta), is a very small wader. It breeds in arctic Europe and Asia, and is a long-distance migrant, wintering south to Africa and south Asia. It occasionally is a vagrant to North America and to Australia. The genus name is from Ancient Greek kalidris or skalidris, a term used by Aristotle for some grey-coloured waterside birds. The specific minuta is Latin for \"small.","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calidris minuta","cells":[[-18.3,22.1,1],[-19.6,22.1,1],[-21.0,13.7,1],[-21.0,14.4,1],[-18.3,17.2,2],[-18.3,21.4,1],[-21.6,16.5,1],[-19.0,13.0,1],[-19.0,16.5,1],[-21.6,15.8,1],[-21.0,15.1,1],[-19.0,17.2,1],[-17.6,20.0,1],[-18.3,16.5,2],[-19.6,15.8,1],[-19.0,15.8,1],[-15.6,34.8,1],[-18.3,30.6,1],[-21.0,32.0,1],[-15.6,32.0,1],[-15.6,29.2,1],[-15.6,28.5,1],[-19.6,22.1,1],[-19.6,22.9,1],[-18.3,24.3,1],[-21.6,35.5,1],[-18.3,23.6,1],[-20.3,25.0,1],[-20.3,24.3,1],[-15.6,27.8,1],[-17.6,25.0,1],[-17.6,24.3,1],[-18.3,32.7,1],[-17.6,25.7,1],[-20.3,25.7,1],[-21.6,23.6,1],[-16.3,34.8,2],[-19.0,26.4,1],[-19.0,23.6,2],[-16.3,29.2,1],[-19.0,34.8,1],[-19.0,27.1,1],[-19.0,34.1,1],[-17.6,30.6,1],[-32.2,20.0,1],[-33.4,20.0,1],[-33.4,22.1,1],[-28.6,16.5,1],[-31.1,17.2,1],[-34.0,20.0,1],[-24.2,15.8,1],[-34.0,21.4,1],[-34.0,20.7,2],[-27.4,15.8,1],[-21.6,16.5,1],[-32.2,20.7,2],[-22.3,17.2,2],[-32.8,18.6,2],[-24.2,16.5,1],[-25.5,20.7,1],[-22.3,14.4,2],[-21.6,15.8,1],[-34.0,19.3,1],[-26.7,17.9,1],[-34.6,19.3,2],[-34.6,20.0,2],[-26.7,15.1,1],[-33.4,18.6,2],[-34.0,18.6,3],[-34.6,18.6,1],[-30.4,22.1,1],[-31.1,22.1,1],[-31.7,17.9,1],[-22.9,14.4,3],[-34.6,20.7,2],[-34.0,22.1,2],[-32.2,18.6,1],[-33.4,17.9,3],[-32.8,17.9,3],[-34.0,22.9,1],[-29.8,25.7,1],[-33.4,22.1,1],[-34.0,25.7,1],[-32.2,29.2,1],[-24.8,27.8,1],[-28.0,27.1,1],[-24.8,29.2,1],[-26.1,27.1,1],[-29.2,30.6,1],[-28.0,26.4,1],[-29.8,30.6,1],[-25.5,28.5,1],[-25.5,27.1,2],[-28.6,32.0,2],[-26.1,32.7,1],[-26.7,27.1,1],[-26.1,29.2,1],[-26.1,27.8,1],[-28.6,25.0,1],[-26.7,32.0,1],[-2